WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:03.360
The cruelty of humanity might be more disturbing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:06.734
than anything Pennywise the&nbsp;
Dancing Clown has ever done.

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:12.320
Fans of horror cinema enjoy being chilled to&nbsp;
the bone with ghastly and disturbing imagery.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:16.720
But to effectively spook an audience, the&nbsp;
filmmakers must ensure that the atmosphere&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:22.560
of fear is cultivated with a steady build-up&nbsp;
of growing anxiety and dread. A scary face just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:27.120
popping up out of nowhere isn't legitimately&nbsp;
terrifying -- it's a cheap jump scare. By the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:31.600
middle of "It," audiences are fully aware of the&nbsp;
horrors that await the group of youngsters who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:36.000
affectionately dubbed themselves The Losers&nbsp;
Club. For all they know, they are recounting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:41.500
spooked hallucinations to one another that may&nbsp;
have amounted to simple nightmares or bad dreams.

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:42.620
“I don’t wanna go missing either.”

00:00:43.457 --> 00:00:44.367
“He has a point.”

00:00:44.367 --> 00:00:48.960
Eventually, the group of outcasts starts to&nbsp;
believe something sinister is actually happening,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:51.920
and that it's all connected to&nbsp;
their little town of Derry. In&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:56.400
one horrific scene, they all experience&nbsp;
the undeniable terror that is Pennywise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.400 --> 00:01:00.560
when he stalks them and lunges for them&nbsp;
out of the projector in Bill's garage.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:05.200
It's a chilling moment that begins subtly&nbsp;
after the projector runs wild with photos&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:10.240
and lands on one of Bill's family. Georgie is&nbsp;
smiling and his mother's face is covered by her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:14.960
hair in the wind. She morphs into the hideous&nbsp;
clown. Many viewers claim this was, perhaps,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:19.920
the single most terrifying moment from the entire&nbsp;
film series. To put it succinctly, a Redditor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:24.901
claimed the scene messed them up entirely. We&nbsp;
can all probably agree with that sentiment.

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:30.240
The most impactful kind of horror comes when&nbsp;
innocent youngsters are subjected to terror.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:34.880
Child casualties are simply far more heinous&nbsp;
and shocking, and the narrative allows even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:39.040
adults to witness the horror from a child's&nbsp;
perspective. "It" does not shy away from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:44.080
targeting young kids at all. In fact, Pennywise&nbsp;
typically satisfies its hunger by feasting on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:48.880
the flesh of the youngsters after the creature&nbsp;
has given them a proper scare. Many fans are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:53.600
still traumatized over poor Georgie's fate&nbsp;
at the hands of the maniacal dancing clown.

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:58.720
The updated "It" movie more accurately portrays&nbsp;
Georgie's demise in all of its grisly detail than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:04.000
the 1990 miniseries ever did. Because of this,&nbsp;
the scene does its job well in making the viewers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:09.280
feel something for the characters. Hopefully, that&nbsp;
something is a mix of dread, horror, and sadness.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:13.840
Even after Pennywise grabs the gravely wounded&nbsp;
little tyke and drags him into the sewer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:18.720
everything from that point on is left up to the&nbsp;
viewers' imaginations. A Reddit user explained&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:23.760
how that is probably the scariest thing about the&nbsp;
scene, as everyone knows the ultimate outcome for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:29.040
Georgie, but what exactly did Pennywise do to him?&nbsp;
The user's thoughts over the matter linger on,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:34.560
debating whether the boy suffered even more before&nbsp;
his final demise or if it was quick and painless.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:37.840
It's also both horrifying and&nbsp;
sad to ponder because these are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:42.000
the very same thoughts that would torment&nbsp;
Georgie's older brother, Bill, to no end.

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:47.600
For obvious reasons, some fans were distraught&nbsp;
by the depiction of homophobia manifesting itself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:52.000
violently at the beginning of "It: Chapter&nbsp;
Two." The film begins 27 years after the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:57.360
events of the first movie. A man by the name of&nbsp;
Adrian Mellon and his boyfriend, Don Hagarty,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:02.400
are enjoying local carnival festivities in Derry&nbsp;
when they are accosted by other locals who insult&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:07.520
them over their sexuality. These locals turn&nbsp;
violent and begin to brutally assault the couple,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:12.800
even going so far as to toss Adrian over a&nbsp;
bridge into the rushing waters of a river below.

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:17.520
After Don rushes to his aid below the bridge,&nbsp;
he sees Pennywise carrying the injured Adrian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:22.720
and then viciously eating the man's heart in a&nbsp;
gruesome display. One Redditor acknowledged that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:26.880
the assault was so horrific that they&nbsp;
felt physically repulsed to watch it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:30.160
Another Reddit user explained how they&nbsp;
fainted when they saw it in the theater,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:33.920
while others discussed the negative&nbsp;
reactions from audiences towards the scene.

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:38.640
The moment was pulled directly from the&nbsp;
novel and was indicative of the level of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:42.800
hatred that courses through Derry thanks&nbsp;
to the emerging influence of Pennywise.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:46.400
Given that the future setting in&nbsp;
the novel was actually in the 1980s,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:52.000
it also recalls a time when the attitudes toward&nbsp;
the LGBTQ+ community were less than accepting.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:56.400
After all, the scene does include the vicious&nbsp;
assault of a human as the result of a hate crime,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.400 --> 00:04:00.849
which should rightfully stir up emotions&nbsp;
and feelings with real-world parallels.

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:06.480
When one messes with the forces of an ancient&nbsp;
cosmic entity looking out for its own survival,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:09.760
casualties are bound to happen,&nbsp;
unfortunately. Aside from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:14.320
countless children and Henry's bully underlings&nbsp;
that became victims of the horrifying clown,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:18.560
the first real casualty of the Losers occurs&nbsp;
at the beginning of "It: Chapter Two."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.560 --> 00:04:22.720
Stanley receives the fated phone call from&nbsp;
Mike telling him that "it" has returned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:27.360
and that the crew needs to reassemble. The&nbsp;
haunting memories from childhood flood back,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:32.434
resulting in Stanley taking his own life so that&nbsp;
he doesn't have to face Pennywise once again.

00:04:32.434 --> 00:04:38.640
“An oath is an oath. Losers…&nbsp;
gotta stick together, right?”

00:04:38.640 --> 00:04:43.520
The rest of the Losers arrive in Derry and spend&nbsp;
time refamiliarizing themselves with the town and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.520 --> 00:04:48.800
their old friendships. After finally realizing&nbsp;
what truly must be done, they attack Pennywise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:53.840
on his home turf. The creature is far stronger&nbsp;
now than before and even manages to deliver a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.840 --> 00:04:59.440
fatal blow to Eddie during the struggle. Fans were&nbsp;
endeared by Eddie who was a chronic hypochondriac&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:04.640
typically afraid of his own shadow. But he musters&nbsp;
all the strength he can to combat his worst fears,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.640 --> 00:05:09.120
ultimately sacrificing himself for the cause.&nbsp;
Richie clearly holds a deep connection with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:13.680
Eddie -- possibly beyond mere friendship&nbsp;
and is completely broken up over the loss.

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:17.280
A Redditor commented how Eddie's death&nbsp;
and Richie's grief were heartbreaking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:22.160
and impacted them for days afterwards due to&nbsp;
the overall sadness. It is truly an upsetting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:26.910
loss for fans who've intimately come to love and&nbsp;
root for these characters and their struggle.

